sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Biller as Biller<br/>utility, landlord, merchant
    participant BB as Biller's bank
    participant Net as Instant network
    participant PB as Payer's bank
    participant Payer

    Note over Biller,Payer: Request to Pay inverts the ask<br/>without inverting the money movement
    Biller->>BB: Create request<br/>amount, due date, reference
    BB->>Net: pain.013 Request to Pay<br/>or UPI collect request
    Net->>PB: Deliver request
    PB->>Payer: Push notification<br/>"ACME Energy requests 84.20,<br/>due 15 Sep"

    alt Payer accepts
        Payer->>PB: Approve and authenticate
        PB->>Net: pacs.008 credit push
        Net->>BB: Payment delivered and settled
        BB->>Biller: Paid, matched to the<br/>original request reference
        Note over Biller: Reconciliation is exact.<br/>The payment carries the invoice ID.
    else Payer declines
        Payer->>PB: Decline
        PB->>Net: pain.014 negative response
        Net->>BB: Declined
        BB->>Biller: No payment. No failed<br/>direct debit fee, no return code.
    else Payer part-pays or defers
        Payer->>PB: Pay 40 now, rest later
        PB->>Net: pacs.008 for 40
        Note over Biller: The scheme allows what a<br/>direct debit never could:<br/>negotiation before the debit.
    end

    Note over Biller,Payer: Why it matters: the payer keeps control,<br/>so the unauthorised-debit dispute<br/>disappears. Why adoption lags:<br/>billers must rebuild dunning,<br/>and the payer can always say no.

    rect rgb(240, 244, 248)
        Note over Net: Scheme names for the same idea:<br/>RTP Request for Payment,<br/>FedNow Request for Payment,<br/>UPI collect and AutoPay mandates,<br/>Pix Automatico and Pix Cobranca,<br/>SEPA Request to Pay
    end
